1
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:09,020
And reverse the spin on the antiproton...

2
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:12,670
and γ becomes α...

3
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:17,620
Multiplied by a matrix of (-i,0)...

4
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:20,010
And there we have it.

5
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:25,310
Conclusive proof that I am absolutely worthless after 9 o'clock.

6
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:31,150
Sheldon...

7
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,360
Sheldon...

8
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:54,450
All right, all right.

9
00:00:54,450 --> 00:00:56,280
I see what's going on.

10
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:59,920
A little pre-Halloween hijinkery.

11
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:09,160
A ghostly moan,

12
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:11,230
a rattling of chains,

13
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:13,230
a witch's cackle.

14
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:17,070
The trifecta of haunted house cliche.

15
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:20,140
Instead of "eek," I say, "yawn."

16
00:01:22,410 --> 00:01:26,150
Sheldon...

17
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:32,120
Oh, the walls are dripping blood,

18
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:35,320
which looks nothing like a phenolphthalein indicator

19
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:38,360
exposed to a sodium carbonate solution.

20
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:44,680
"See you in hell Sheldon."

21
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:49,290
The most frightening thing about that is the missing comma.

22
00:01:53,270 --> 00:01:55,940
Okay, all right.

23
00:01:56,340 --> 00:01:58,280
That one was clever.

24
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:01,810
Skeleton with phosphorous on a zip line.

25
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:04,550
Come on out, merry pranksters.

26
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:06,620
Take a bow.

27
00:02:10,730 --> 00:02:12,390
You should've seen your face.

28
00:02:12,390 --> 00:02:16,160
Yes, there's nothing quite like the slightly widened eyes

29
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:18,400
of mildly startled.

30
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:19,790
Come on, admit it.

31
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:20,960
We got you, Sheldon.

32
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:24,720
Please, fright depends on an element of surprise.

33
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,060
The simple fact is,

34
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:28,070
because I am much smarter than you,

35
00:02:28,070 --> 00:02:30,300
and able to anticipate your actions,

36
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,860
it is highly unlikely that you two rubes

37
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:34,880
could ever surprise me.

38
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:36,880
He's probably right.

39
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:39,700
We can't beat him. He's just too smart.

40
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:40,760
Gentlemen.

41
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,430
Who had money on "faints"?

42
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:50,580
I had "pee his pants."

43
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:51,820
Hang on.

44
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:54,010
Looks like everyone's a winner.

45
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:19,970
Oh. Watch out, Sheldon.

46
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:23,810
This little boy Casper is a g-g-g-ghost!

47
00:03:24,570 --> 00:03:25,970
Droll.

48
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:27,810
Not as droll as a grown man

49
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:30,010
passed out in a puddle of his own urine.

50
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:33,050
That was pretty droll.

51
00:03:33,050 --> 00:03:34,880
With a hint of ammonia.

52
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:39,010
Yes, enjoy your japes, gentlemen.

53
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:41,750
You think you've poked fun at a milquetoast academic.

54
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:43,350
Well, you've forgotten one thing:

55
00:03:43,350 --> 00:03:45,720
I am also a son of the Lone Star state.

56
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:47,890
I'm Texas through and through.

57
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:50,640
And we know how to settle scores down there.

58
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:54,310
If you doubt me, ask Mexico.

59
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,260
Hot girl, nine o'clock.

60
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:02,400
Don't everybody look at once!

61
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:06,210
What is she doing in a comic book store?

62
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:10,090
I don't know, she might be lost.

63
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:14,800
Doesn't matter. Watch and learn.

64
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:21,760
- Hi.  - Hi.

65
00:04:24,090 --> 00:04:26,820
... it-it-it...

66
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:35,070
Shut up.

67
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:38,700
Are you getting this Next Men?

68
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:40,600
Uh, yeah. It's issue number 21.

69
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:41,810
First appearance of Hellboy.

70
00:04:41,810 --> 00:04:44,540
I know. I've been looking for it for years.

71
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:47,610
- Sorry.  - Hey, if I pretended to hit on you,

72
00:04:47,610 --> 00:04:50,510
could I distract you enough to sneak it away?

73
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:55,090
Yes, but you'd be using your superpowers for evil.

74
00:04:55,090 --> 00:04:58,820
Damn, I'm forbidden by my Kryptonian father to do so.

75
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:01,330
I'm Alice.

76
00:05:01,330 --> 00:05:02,690
Leonard.

77
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:04,430
You're very cute, Leonard.

78
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:05,100
Thanks. You, too.

79
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,100
You know, go ahead and take it.

80
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,200
No, no. No, no, I-I did evil.

81
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,070
Would you be open to a trade?

82
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:14,840
Yeah, yeah, sure, I guess.

83
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,210
Okay. Here.

84
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:18,410
This is my number.

85
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:19,880
Call me.

86
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:22,350
Sorry, palm's a little sweaty.

87
00:05:22,350 --> 00:05:23,580
What's that word?

88
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:26,620
- Alice.  - Oh, right, your name.

89
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:28,990
That makes more sense than "Penis".

90
00:05:30,190 --> 00:05:31,680
Later.

91
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:37,290
Did we just see you pick up a girl in a comic book store?

92
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,360
'Cause if you did, you get your picture up there

93
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:41,230
on the Wall of Heroes.

94
00:05:41,230 --> 00:05:43,640
No, I don't think I picked her up.

95
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:44,620
Besides, I have a girlfriend.

96
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,770
Doesn't matter. This is the closest anyone's ever come.

97
00:05:46,770 --> 00:05:48,710
You're going on the wall, my friend.

98
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:55,610
Be sure to check the mail.

99
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:57,190
How many times are you gonna tell me?

100
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:58,990
- What's with you? - Nothing.

101
00:05:58,990 --> 00:06:00,880
It's not suspicious that I'm fixating.

102
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,810
It's consistent with my personality.

103
00:06:03,850 --> 00:06:05,070
Right.

104
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:05,720
Hey, guys.

105
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:06,920
More Halloween candy?

106
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,330
Didn't you just buy a bunch of it yesterday?

107
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:10,750
Oh. Yeah. That's gone.

108
00:06:12,530 --> 00:06:14,620
It's a rough month when Halloween and PMS

109
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:16,600
hit at the same time.

110
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,060
Leonard doesn't have time to chat,

111
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,120
he has to get the mail.

112
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,710
Will you relax? I'll get it in a minute.

113
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:24,820
- How was work?  - Open the mail!

114
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:27,310
Excuse me.

115
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:37,730
A couple of circulars, nothing important.

116
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:40,420
- What's with him? - Hang on.

117
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:54,580
You might be from Texas, but I'm from New Jersey.

118
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,140
Check it out.

119
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:03,560
Jim Lee drew this of me two years ago at Comic Con.

120
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,180
What are you wearing?

121
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:07,020
Well, you know, it's Comic Con.

122
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:12,020
I'm Lion-O from ThunderCats.

123
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:15,240
Wow, you must have gotten so laid.

124
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:18,970
No. But Jessica Alba did rub my furry belly.

125
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,570
Want to see a comic I draw?

126
00:07:23,570 --> 00:07:25,650
You're kidding. You have your own book?

127
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:28,160
Yeah. It's kinda based on my life.

128
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,550
Cool.

129
00:07:31,190 --> 00:07:34,090
Oh, look. That's you having sex with a guy

130
00:07:34,090 --> 00:07:37,140
in the top half of a Chewbacca costume.

131
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,210
Comic Con?

132
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:42,370
You'd think, but no.

133
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:46,330
You're very talented. This is really good.

134
00:07:46,330 --> 00:07:47,900
Did you do...

135
00:07:53,250 --> 00:07:56,840
So, can I trade you my comic for the Hellboy?

136
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:59,290
You can have my car.

137
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:15,400
Oh, dear.

138
00:08:17,590 --> 00:08:19,080
Oh, dear...

139
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:24,010
Oh, dear, oh, dear, oh, dear...

140
00:08:24,010 --> 00:08:26,370
Oh, dear, oh, dear, oh, dear.

141
00:08:26,370 --> 00:08:30,110
Purell, Purell, Purell, Purell.

142
00:08:46,490 --> 00:08:47,540
Good morning, Sheldon.

143
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:49,640
It is, isn't it?

144
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:59,020
Oh, bother.

145
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:01,000
Isn't that just always the way?

146
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,730
You go to staple something, and you're out of staples.

147
00:09:03,730 --> 00:09:05,940
Gosh, I wish I'd known that earlier today

148
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:08,630
when I was at Staples.

149
00:09:09,310 --> 00:09:11,860
You ever think of paper clips right there?

150
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:16,430
No, no, I need something more permanent to join these papers.

151
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:21,410
Say, don't you keep staples in your top desk drawer?

152
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:23,170
I don't know. Maybe.

153
00:09:23,810 --> 00:09:26,270
Be a lamb and check.

154
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:28,690
All right.

155
00:09:31,770 --> 00:09:34,480
Who do we have here?

156
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:39,110
It's a snake. A terrifying snake.

157
00:09:39,110 --> 00:09:43,210
Oh, did some bad man put us in a drawer?

158
00:09:43,210 --> 00:09:44,760
Stop talking like that.

159
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:47,540
You've been rendered speechless by fear.

160
00:09:48,330 --> 00:09:49,760
Let's go to the biology lab

161
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:53,630
and find you some nice yummy mice.

162
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:58,230
I tried to scare an Indian with a snake.

163
00:09:58,970 --> 00:10:01,610
Come on, Cooper. You're better than this.

164
00:10:05,510 --> 00:10:06,780
It's open.

165
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,160
Hey, you got a minute?

166
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,490
Yeah, sure, come on in.

167
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:12,260
Thanks.

168
00:10:12,730 --> 00:10:13,950
Want some mac and cheese?

169
00:10:13,950 --> 00:10:15,870
No. Lactose. Gas.

170
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:20,270
- Glass of wine?  - No. Sulfites. Migraines.

171
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:22,640
Okay, well, I'd offer you Halloween candy,

172
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:24,420
but that's gone.

173
00:10:25,330 --> 00:10:26,660
So, what's up?

174
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:28,830
Okay, we used to go out, right?

175
00:10:28,830 --> 00:10:32,060
Oh, my God, that's where I know you from.

176
00:10:33,430 --> 00:10:34,940
I'm dealing with a situation

177
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:37,340
and it's kind of about my love life,

178
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:40,010
so I know that might be weird for us to talk about,

179
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:41,240
but in this area, as you know,

180
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:44,980
all my other friends are just so stupid.

181
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:47,080
All right, what's going on?

182
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,680
So, you're okay talking about this?

183
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:50,150
- Yes. - You're sure it's not weird.

184
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:51,580
It's okay.

185
00:10:51,590 --> 00:10:53,060
You know what, if you ever want to talk to me

186
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:55,060
about a problem in your life with a guy,

187
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:56,660
then I would be fine with that.

188
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,460
Okay, good, because there's this one guy I used to date

189
00:10:58,460 --> 00:11:00,060
who's about to be force-fed wine and cheese

190
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:01,760
if he doesn't get to the point.

191
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,730
Okay,

192
00:11:04,730 --> 00:11:06,570
here it is.

193
00:11:06,570 --> 00:11:08,940
Is it cheating if a guy has a girlfriend...

194
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,800
Yeah, probably.

195
00:11:12,730 --> 00:11:13,290
Come on.

196
00:11:13,290 --> 00:11:14,430
I'm sorry, go ahead.

197
00:11:14,810 --> 00:11:17,030
I met this girl, and she's great.

198
00:11:17,030 --> 00:11:18,390
we have a lot in common.

199
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:19,690
Did you guys do it?

200
00:11:19,690 --> 00:11:21,790
No. We just made out a little.

201
00:11:21,790 --> 00:11:25,140
Oh, look at you, you bad boy.

202
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:26,340
Did you tell her about Priya?

203
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:30,050
Well, I was gonna, but there were too many tongues in my mouth.

204
00:11:31,940 --> 00:11:33,030
That's gross.

205
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:36,940
Here's the thing,

206
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:39,140
I-I'm not one of those guys who sneaks around

207
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:41,070
and sleeps with more than one woman.

208
00:11:41,070 --> 00:11:42,170
Well, good for you.

209
00:11:42,170 --> 00:11:45,070
The problem is, I want to be one of those guys.

210
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:48,780
So sleep with the new girl and lie to Priya.

211
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:50,380
Oh, that's not who I am.

212
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:52,680
All right, then break it off with the new girl.

213
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:54,180
Now, let's not do anything rash.

214
00:11:54,190 --> 00:11:56,290
She's really hot.

215
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:57,890
If you like this girl so much,

216
00:11:57,890 --> 00:11:59,690
why don't you just end things with Priya?

217
00:12:00,210 --> 00:12:01,290
Priya and I are in love.

218
00:12:01,290 --> 00:12:03,620
I think we could get married someday.

219
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:06,220
Leonard, you're looking for a way to sleep with both women

220
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:07,940
and have everybody be happy about it.

221
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:09,910
Now we're getting somewhere.

222
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:14,750
What does your gut tell you?

223
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:17,380
"Go ask Penny; she'll know what to do."

224
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:27,730
Hello, Howard.

225
00:12:27,730 --> 00:12:31,540
I've realized that you scaring me was all in jest.

226
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:35,120
Allow me to say, job well done.

227
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:48,030
Perfect.

228
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:52,880
What are you doing?

229
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:55,310
Science. You wouldn't understand.

230
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:59,210
Hey, well, see you. I'm going out.

231
00:13:06,850 --> 00:13:09,640
I thought you were leaving the apartment.

232
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:12,460
Yeah, me, too. I can't make up my mind.

233
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,730
Are you concerned because the world is filled

234
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:16,850
with big dogs and bullies?

235
00:13:18,570 --> 00:13:21,850
No. I'm having a moral crisis.

236
00:13:21,850 --> 00:13:23,760
Well, if it's of any help,

237
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:26,930
I've read all the great moral philosophers,

238
00:13:26,930 --> 00:13:29,200
including Dr. Seuss.

239
00:13:31,290 --> 00:13:32,810
Oh, what the hell.

240
00:13:33,530 --> 00:13:34,600
I'm supposed to go see that girl

241
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,800
from the comic book store, Alice,

242
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,990
but I don't know if I should,

243
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:39,120
because I'm going out with Priya,

244
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,730
but she's in India.

245
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:45,780
All right. So the topic at hand is sexual fidelity.

246
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:48,430
Probably won't be relying on Seuss here.

247
00:13:49,290 --> 00:13:51,400
Although One Fish, Two Fish, Red Fish, Blue Fish

248
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,650
might be surprisingly applicable.

249
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:56,530
Go on.

250
00:13:56,530 --> 00:13:57,450
Well...

251
00:13:57,450 --> 00:13:59,190
they say at the end of your life,

252
00:13:59,190 --> 00:14:00,720
you regret the stuff you didn't do

253
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,410
more than the stuff that you did,

254
00:14:02,410 --> 00:14:06,400
and I'm pretty sure Alice is the stuff I want to do.

255
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:11,510
You know, the German philosopher, Friedrich Nietzsche,

256
00:14:11,510 --> 00:14:14,980
believed that morality is just a fiction

257
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:17,750
used by the herd of inferior human beings

258
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:21,690
to hold back the few superior men.

259
00:14:21,690 --> 00:14:24,040
That actually does help.

260
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:27,110
It's worth noting that he died of syphilis.

261
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:33,900
- Screw it, I'm going.   - On your way home,

262
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:36,170
- will you pick up some orange juice? - Do you mind?

263
00:14:36,170 --> 00:14:38,210
I'm questioning a lot of things in my life right now.

264
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:42,080
Is one of those things your fondness for orange juice?

265
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:44,500
- No.  - Great. Tropicana, no pulp.

266
00:14:53,490 --> 00:14:54,560
Hey, Sheldon.

267
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,260
Who is it!

268
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,570
It's me, Sheldon, Mrs. Wolowitz.

269
00:14:58,570 --> 00:15:01,690
That's not my mom, it's Bernadette.

270
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:06,390
Really? That's very unsettling.

271
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:07,950
Hi, Sheldon.

272
00:15:07,950 --> 00:15:10,770
- Hi.  - What's up?

273
00:15:10,770 --> 00:15:14,300
It just occurred to me that I never formally congratulated you

274
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:15,720
on your pending nuptials.

275
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:16,760
So I hopped on

276
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:20,400
the first bus and hightailed it down here to shake your hand.

277
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:23,180
Put 'er there, you old so-and-so.

278
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:26,760
Well, I-I'm gonna see you at work in...12 hours

279
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,450
don't you think it could have waited until then?

280
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:33,330
Holy smoke, why didn't I think of that?

281
00:15:33,330 --> 00:15:35,570
You're a better man than I, Howard Wolowitz.

282
00:15:35,570 --> 00:15:38,140
You put 'er there, you son of a gun!

283
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:40,750
Whatever.

284
00:15:41,710 --> 00:15:43,370
My...oh...

285
00:15:43,370 --> 00:15:45,590
it's...

286
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:48,690
Oh, my God, Howard!

287
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:49,790
What did you do?

288
00:15:49,790 --> 00:15:52,240
It was a harmless Halloween prank. Look.

289
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:55,100
Howard has a heart condition! You know that!

290
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:57,290
Well, I thought he made that up.

291
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,770
I-Isn't hypochondria

292
00:15:58,770 --> 00:16:01,600
a common idiosyncrasy of Jewish people?

293
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,030
This is adrenaline --

294
00:16:06,030 --> 00:16:07,940
we're gonna have to inject it into his heart.

295
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:09,370
- We are?  - You are.

296
00:16:09,370 --> 00:16:11,310
I'm not strong enough to get it through his chest plate,

297
00:16:11,310 --> 00:16:13,500
and we've only got one shot.

298
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:17,040
Oh, no! I can't!

299
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:17,550
Hurry!

300
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:19,630
We're running out of time!

301
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,270
- Okay.  - Just do it!

302
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:23,130
Oh, God!

303
00:16:23,130 --> 00:16:24,990
One...two...

304
00:16:24,990 --> 00:16:26,830
three!

305
00:16:26,830 --> 00:16:29,550
Trick or treat, bubbeleh.

306
00:16:29,550 --> 00:16:30,890
What?

307
00:16:32,390 --> 00:16:35,290
No. You mean this was all a ruse?

308
00:16:35,290 --> 00:16:39,080
Oh, how could I be so stu...

309
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,170
Damn it, I can't.

310
00:16:47,170 --> 00:16:48,720
I can't do this.

311
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,890
Uh, is it my tongue stud?

312
00:16:49,890 --> 00:16:51,060
'Cause if that freaks you out,

313
00:16:51,060 --> 00:16:52,850
you're in for a real surprise later on.

314
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:54,170
No, no, no.

315
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:56,400
I-I can't do this.

316
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:58,610
Believe me, I really want to.

317
00:16:58,610 --> 00:17:01,540
- But...?  - But I kind of have a girlfriend.

318
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:02,580
Are you kidding?

319
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:05,270
You're cool with you and me just being friends, right?

320
00:17:05,270 --> 00:17:06,710
I don't believe this.

321
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:09,740
Wait, I don't... Which part?

322
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:11,410
I'm so stupid.

323
00:17:11,410 --> 00:17:12,690
I thought for once I'd met a good guy,

324
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:14,280
but you're just another jackass.

325
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:17,400
Oh, no, no, you have it wrong.

326
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:19,980
No. I-I was going to be a jackass,

327
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:22,220
but I stopped myself.

328
00:17:22,970 --> 00:17:24,860
I stayed a good guy, so...

329
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:26,830
I'm gonna pass on the sex.

330
00:17:26,830 --> 00:17:30,190
But you should know, that's not a comment on your hotness

331
00:17:30,190 --> 00:17:32,830
but on my goodness.

332
00:17:32,830 --> 00:17:34,360
That's kind of my superpower.

333
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:37,380
I'm, like, Captain Good Guy.

334
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:42,690
It's okay.

335
00:17:42,690 --> 00:17:45,210
Did the right thing.

336
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:48,060
You idiot!

337
00:17:51,310 --> 00:17:52,760
Hey, Priya.

338
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,240
Hey, sweetheart. How's it going?

339
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,440
Uh, not so good.

340
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,740
We have to talk.

341
00:17:56,740 --> 00:18:00,190
Oh, sounds serious. What's up?

342
00:18:00,190 --> 00:18:03,430
Okay, uh...here it is.

343
00:18:03,430 --> 00:18:05,240
I met this girl and I kissed her,

344
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,540
and I feel terrible about it.

345
00:18:06,540 --> 00:18:08,680
But it's done, it's never gonna happen again.

346
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:11,320
And I am so, so sorry.

347
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,920
Leonard, relax.

348
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:13,720
It's okay.

349
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,880
It is?

350
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:16,530
Yeah, these things happen.

351
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:18,740
They happen to everybody.

352
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:21,770
Oh, my God, you are amazing.

353
00:18:21,770 --> 00:18:23,760
I mean, I don't deserve you.

354
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:26,290
Wh-what do you mean "everybody"?

355
00:18:28,430 --> 00:18:31,140
Leonard, I didn't know if I should tell you,

356
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:34,330
but I kind of cheated on you, too.

357
00:18:34,330 --> 00:18:36,870
Kind of?

358
00:18:37,430 --> 00:18:39,420
A couple of weeks ago,

359
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:42,460
I slept with my ex-boyfriend.

360
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:45,460
So, I guess we both messed up a little.

361
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:50,660
No, no, I messed up a little. You messed up a lot.

362
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:52,920
Well, it's not a competition.

363
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:57,990
Oh...yeah, it is, and you won.

364
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:01,560
I-I-I'm sorry, I have to go.

365
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:05,380
I don't believe this.

366
00:19:16,850 --> 00:19:19,920
Bazinga, punk. Now we're even.

